<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<handout>
  <title>Section 3.5: Properties and Applications of Logarithms</title>

  <sidebyside widths="45% 45%">
    <p><md>y = 10^t ~~~ \iff ~~~ \log_{10}(\underline{\ \ \ \ }) = {\underline{\ \ \ \ }}</md>
<md>\log_{10}(10^t) = {\underline{\ \ \ \ }}</md>
<md>10^{\log_{10}(y)} = {\underline{\ \ \ \ }}</md></p>
    <p><md>y = e^t ~~~ \iff ~~~ \ln(\underline{\ \ \ \ }) = {\underline{\ \ \ \ }}</md>
<md>\ln(e^t) = {\underline{\ \ \ \ }}</md>
<md>e^{\ln(y)} = {\underline{\ \ \ \ }}</md></p>
  </sidebyside>

  <assemblage>
    <title>Property 1</title>
    <p>Multiplication inside logs.</p>
  </assemblage>

  <assemblage>
    <title>Property 2</title>
    <p>Division inside logs.</p>
  </assemblage>

  <assemblage>
    <title>Property 3</title>
    <p>Powers inside logs.</p>
  </assemblage>

  <p workspace="0.15in">* Use to solve any exponential function, regardless of base!</p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>Class ex: <m>4^t = 7</m></cell>
      <cell>Class ex: <m>7\cdot 3^{2t}=6</m></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell></cell>
      <cell></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell></cell>
      <cell></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell></cell>
      <cell></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell></cell>
      <cell></cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <activity>
    <title>Activity 3.5.2</title>
    <introduction>
      <p>Solve each of the following equations <term>exactly</term> and then find an estimate that is accurate to 5 decimal places.</p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="4cm">
      <statement>
        <p><m>3^t = 5</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="4cm">
      <statement>
        <p><m>4\cdot 2^t-2=3</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="4cm">
      <statement>
        <p><m>3.7\cdot(0.9)^{0.3t}+1.5 = 2.1</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="4cm">
      <statement>
        <p><m>72 - 30(0.7)^{0.05t}=60</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="4cm">
      <statement>
        <p><m>\ln(t)=-2</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="4cm">
      <statement>
        <p><m>3+2\log_{10}(t)=3.5</m></p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </activity>

  <image source="images/3.5g.png" width="50%"/>

  <assemblage>
    <title>The graph of <m>y=\ln(x)</m></title>
    <p>Graph <m>e^x</m> is shown above the line <m>y=x</m>, and <m>\ln(x)</m> is shown below the line <m>y=x</m>. Left is zoomed in, right is zoomed out.</p>
    <p>The graph of <m>y=\ln(x)</m>:</p>
    <p>
      <ul>
        <li><p>vertical asymptote at <m>x=0</m></p></li>
        <li><p>passes through <m>(1,0)</m></p></li>
        <li><p>is always increasing</p></li>
        <li><p>is always concave down</p></li>
        <li><p>increases without bound</p></li>
      </ul>
    </p>
  </assemblage>

  <activity>
    <title>Activity 3.5.3</title>
    <introduction>
      <p>In the questions that follow, we compare and contrast the properties and behaviors of exponential and logarithmic functions.</p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="1cm">
      <statement>
        <p>Go to Desmos and plot <m>f(x)=-e^{-(x-1)}+1</m>
 and <m>g(x) = \ln(x)</m>.
 Compare the properties of the two, noting what they have in common and what they don't.</p>
